aquinas-will-antecedent.md:1: argue/answered: S3: answered no, which keeps aquinas-will-antecedent.logic.r1.2 and aquinas-will-antecedent.logic.r1.3, to: Suppose "God wills the thing" is true and "the thing is necessary by its antecedent cause" is false. Is S3, "Now things created by God are related to the divine will as to an antecedent cause, whereby they have necessity.", true then?
